.SH "NAME"
ll2_new_context \- Allocates context which defines the lastlog2 environment.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
\fB#include <lastlog2.h>\fP
.sp
*ll2_context * ll2_new_context(const char *\fIdb_path\fP);
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
Defines lastlog2 context e.g. database file, which will be used for
any other lastlog2 call. If \fIdb_path\fP is NULL, the default path defined
in \fILL2_DEFAULT_DATABASE\fP will be taken.
.sp
.if n .RS 4
.nf
.fam C
const\&   char *db_path = "/var/lib/lastlog/lastlog2.db";
ll2_context *context = ll2_new_context(db_path);
.fam
.fi
.if n .RE
.SH "RETURN VALUE"
.sp
Returns context which will be used for all other lastlog2 library calls.
This context should be released with \fIll2_unref_context\fP when it is not
needed anymore.
Returns NULL on an error.
